{
 "cells": [
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Week 9 (Wed) - Plotting in Python "
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "This project will introduce you to working with and plotting/respresenting data.\n",
    "(Written by P. Frinchaboy, M. Bovill, and J. Donor)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### Plotting data is one of the easiest way to determine if something may be odd/wonrg with your data.  \n",
    "\n",
    "Also visuallying data is a key way to help interpret things in science (__e.g., a picture is worth a thousand words, especially when your data is 100,000+ data points!__). "
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 3,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "data = np.genfromtxt(\"munich_temperatures_average_with_bad_data1.txt\")\n",
    "from matplotlib import pyplot as plt \n",
    "#matplotlib.pyplot is the standard for making plots and is derived from Matlab\n",
    "import numpy as np"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### Lets plot our data from last class!!!  YAY WE GET TO FINALLY MAKE PLOTS!"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 5,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [
    {
     "data": {
      "image/png": "",
      "text/plain": [
       "<Figure size 2000x1000 with 1 Axes>"
      ]
     },
     "metadata": {},
     "output_type": "display_data"
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "# READ IN DATA FILE\n",
    "data = np.genfromtxt(\"munich_temperatures_average_with_bad_data1.txt\")\n",
    "Date = data[:,0]\n",
    "Temp = data[:,1]\n",
    "\n",
    "# PLOT DATA\n",
    "fig1 = plt.figure(figsize=(20,10))\n",
    "ax1 = fig1.add_subplot(111)\n",
    "\n",
    "ax1.scatter(Date, Temp, s=15, c='k', alpha=0.5)\n",
    "\n",
    "ax1.xaxis.set_tick_params(labelsize=20)\n",
    "ax1.yaxis.set_tick_params(labelsize=20)\n",
    "\n",
    "plt.show()"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## A new plot\n",
    "\n",
    "You will first need to download the plain text data file \"CG20.dat\", that we will read in to have data to plot."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 6,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# This will read in the data into a numpy array\n",
    "data = np.genfromtxt(\"CG20.csv\", delimiter=\",\")\n",
    "# This will seperate specific columns of the data into newly created variables\n",
    "AgeNN = data[:,14]  # Log Age \n",
    "DistPc = data[:,17] # Distance\n",
    "XGC = data[:,18]   # X-coordinate\n",
    "YGC = data[:,19]   # Y-coordinate\n",
    "ZGC = data[:,20]   # Z-coordinate\n",
    "RGC = data[:,21]   # Radius-coordinate\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "__Next will will gerenerate a first plot of X vs Y position.__\n",
    "\n",
    "This will introduce the first options you will have."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 7,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [
    {
     "data": {
      "text/plain": [
       "<matplotlib.collections.PathCollection at 0x14b359f90>"
      ]
     },
     "execution_count": 7,
     "metadata": {},
     "output_type": "execute_result"
    },
    {
     "data": {
      "image/png": "",
      "text/plain": [
       "<Figure size 640x480 with 1 Axes>"
      ]
     },
     "metadata": {},
     "output_type": "display_data"
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "# Creating a scatter plot in log log space using an object oriented approach\n",
    "fig = plt.figure()                           # makes a figure\n",
    "ax = fig.add_subplot(111)                    # make a 1,1,1 (single) figure\n",
    "ax.scatter(XGC,YGC,s=5,c='k',alpha=0.3)      # makes a scatter plot (s = size, c = color, alpha = transparency)\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 8,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [
    {
     "data": {
      "text/plain": [
       "<matplotlib.collections.PathCollection at 0x14b870a50>"
      ]
     },
     "execution_count": 8,
     "metadata": {},
     "output_type": "execute_result"
    },
    {
     "data": {
      "image/png": "",
      "text/plain": [
       "<Figure size 1600x1000 with 1 Axes>"
      ]
     },
     "metadata": {},
     "output_type": "display_data"
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "# Changing the size of the plot -- figsize\n",
    "fig = plt.figure(figsize=(16,10))          # makes a figure (allow us to change the size of the figure)\n",
    "ax = fig.add_subplot(111)                  # make a 1,1,1 (single) figure\n",
    "ax.scatter(XGC,YGC,s=5,c='k',alpha=0.3)    # makes a scatter plot (s = size, c = color, alpha = transparency)\n",
    "\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "Well this looks like a nice plot, but if you gave this to someone could they tell what it was a plot of?\n",
    "\n",
    "We need add labels to inform the reader, also we will limit the plot to only show a portion of the data."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 9,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [
    {
     "name": "stdout",
     "output_type": "stream",
     "text": [
      "('Cluster', 'RAdeg', 'DEdeg', 'GLON', 'GLAT', 'r50', 'nbstars07', 'pmRA', 'e_pmRA', 'pmDE', 'e_pmDE', 'plx', 'e_plx', 'Flag', 'AgeNN', 'AVNN', 'DMNN', 'DistPc', 'X', 'Y', 'Z', 'Rgc')\n"
     ]
    },
    {
     "data": {
      "image/png": "",
      "text/plain": [
       "<Figure size 1600x1000 with 1 Axes>"
      ]
     },
     "metadata": {},
     "output_type": "display_data"
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "# Reread the data to get ALL of the columns\n",
    "data = np.genfromtxt(\"CG20.csv\", delimiter=\",\", names = True)\n",
    "\n",
    "print(data.dtype.names)\n",
    "# this is the same as above\n",
    "fig = plt.figure(figsize=(16,10))\n",
    "ax = fig.add_subplot(111)\n",
    "ax.scatter(data['X'],data['Y'],s=20,c='k',alpha=0.3)    # makes a scatter plot (s = size, c = color, alpha = transparency)\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "# Now, we will label the axis and set the limits of the axis and increase ticksize of the axis\n",
    "# Set the start and end of range you want to display on the x and yaxis \n",
    "ax.set_xlim(-2000,2000)\n",
    "ax.set_ylim(-1500,1500)\n",
    "\n",
    "# add the labels\n",
    "ax.set_xlabel(\"$X_{GC}$ $(pc)$\",size=20)   # allows LaTeX style formating\n",
    "ax.set_ylabel(\"$Y_{GC}$ $(pc)$\",size=20)   # allows LaTeX style formating\n",
    "\n",
    "# increase the size of the numbers on the axes\n",
    "ax.xaxis.set_tick_params(labelsize=20)\n",
    "ax.yaxis.set_tick_params(labelsize=20)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 10,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [
    {
     "data": {
      "image/png": "",
      "text/plain": [
       "<Figure size 1600x1000 with 1 Axes>"
      ]
     },
     "metadata": {},
     "output_type": "display_data"
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "# this is the same as above\n",
    "fig = plt.figure(figsize=(16,10))\n",
    "ax = fig.add_subplot(111)\n",
    "\n",
    "# Sizing the points according to a 3rd attribute - rvir\n",
    "ax.scatter(data['X'],data['Y'],s=200*data['r50'],c='k',alpha=0.3)  \n",
    "\n",
    "# Now, we will label the axis and set the limits of the axis and increase ticksize of the axis\n",
    "# Set the start and end of range you want to display on the x and yaxis \n",
    "ax.set_xlim(-2000,2000)\n",
    "ax.set_ylim(-1500,1500)\n",
    "\n",
    "# add the labels\n",
    "ax.set_xlabel(\"$X_{GC}$ $(pc)$\",size=20)   # allows LaTeX style formating\n",
    "ax.set_ylabel(\"$Y_{GC}$ $(pc)$\",size=20)   # allows LaTeX style formating\n",
    "\n",
    "# increase the size of the numbers on the axes\n",
    "ax.xaxis.set_tick_params(labelsize=20)\n",
    "ax.yaxis.set_tick_params(labelsize=20)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 11,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [
    {
     "data": {
      "image/png": "",
      "text/plain": [
       "<Figure size 1600x1000 with 2 Axes>"
      ]
     },
     "metadata": {},
     "output_type": "display_data"
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "# this is the same as above\n",
    "fig = plt.figure(figsize=(16,10))\n",
    "ax = fig.add_subplot(111)\n",
    "\n",
    "# Coloring the points by a 4th attribute and adding a color bar\n",
    "image = ax.scatter(data['X'],data['Y'],s=200*data['r50'],c=data['AgeNN'],edgecolor='k',cmap=\"viridis\",alpha=0.5)\n",
    "bar = fig.colorbar(image,orientation=\"vertical\",pad=0.01)\n",
    "bar.set_label('$log_{10} (Age)$',size=15)\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "# Now, we will label the axis and set the limits of the axis and increase ticksize of the axis\n",
    "# Set the start and end of range you want to display on the x and yaxis \n",
    "ax.set_xlim(-2000,2000)\n",
    "ax.set_ylim(-1500,1500)\n",
    "\n",
    "# add the labels\n",
    "ax.set_xlabel(\"$X_{GC}$ $(pc)$\",size=20)   # allows LaTeX style formating\n",
    "ax.set_ylabel(\"$Y_{GC}$ $(pc)$\",size=20)   # allows LaTeX style formating\n",
    "\n",
    "# increase the size of the numbers on the axes\n",
    "ax.xaxis.set_tick_params(labelsize=20)\n",
    "ax.yaxis.set_tick_params(labelsize=20)\n",
    "\n",
    "\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 12,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [
    {
     "data": {
